      "MarkerBody": {
        "description": "The 3D shape an electrode marker carries, so the loupe can draw the true solid\n(not just its flat footprint). Dimensions are summarised to what the view needs:\n``radius_um`` is the base/lateral radius, ``height_um`` the depth into the tissue\n(0 for a hemisphere \u2014 its radius is the depth), ``top_radius_um`` the frustum's tip.\nA CAD solid is drawn as its bounding cylinder.",
        "properties": {
          "height_um": {
            "default": 0.0,
            "title": "Height Um",
            "type": "number"
          },
          "kind": {
            "enum": [
              "hemisphere",
              "cylinder",
              "frustum",
              "cad"
